<title>UK: NWE gasoline eases after Tuesday's rise.</title>
<headline>NWE gasoline eases after Tuesday's rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE gasoline slipped back $1 or so on Wednesday after yesterday's $3 a tonne hike. Dealers said extra buying ahead of today's U.K. budget had eased with eurograde barges around $187.00 fob ARA.</p>
<p>Dealers said arbitrage talk was giving the cargo market some backbone and premium unleaded NWE cargoes were assessed around $184.00 fob.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 17 542 8980</p>
